p0_verdicts.restrictions:
Components:
- Frozen COST-criterion outcome (U >= 1.25 not met; scaling extension not triggered): VERIFIED as measured.
- 'No headroom / nothing to amortise' as an interpretation: CONDITIONALLY_VALID.
- 'Any ECRO-class generator makes edits slower (0.92-0.93x)': IMPLEMENTATION_DEFECT; the corrected value is about 0.97x, parity.
- 'No scaling hypothesis reaches 1.25x': UNTESTED_INFERENCE as written.
- Extension to learned operators that own the q table or prefix, or to learned transport in general: UNTESTED_INFERENCE.
The claim holds only when all of the following apply:
(i) the learned element replaces only the three >=3-event orders and still pays for the explicit q table, first order, relation update and frame;
(ii) the lifecycle is synchronised wall time of this Python/Dr.Jit/torch prototype, or any basis keeping the 512^2 x 64-spp frame in the denominator;
(iii) CK2, one point light, J = 4, N = 1,270 (audit runs extend this to 11,430);
(iv) one timing-only rigid edit with no T1 reference, so the ratio is quality-free;
(v) one GPU and one implementation.
Under these conditions the ceiling is 1.02 (edit) / 1.04 (source), and at most 1.13 without the frame. On a GPU-work basis without a frame it is about 1.6 (idealised). For a full learned operator the derived, quality-unmatched source ceiling is 1.24-1.37 on wall.
